#uuid "62b0afc9-a32f-57ab-a5e5-798d366d7640" :question/math-academy-id "q-127078" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y+8}{-4}=\\frac{z+1}{11}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y-(-8)}{-4}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{11},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(10,-8,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨7,-4,11⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127078/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9927bff1-c245-542b-8d5d-fa7d24188b85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70866/selection/f40d67ee259364150135dfbb2a64c46be6deb0cf2fc51eb62b1f8caf26b03b92" :answer/id #uuid "42dadc7d-c9c1-545b-a8b8-8605b85939eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-11-4t \\\\ y=3+5t \\\\ z=1+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70866/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "946e1639-1084-582e-8d76-e37f2f31c936" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70866/selection/ec67142989558c2cfdd9d6a0854a